<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>



<PLUGIN
  name="docktail"
  author="vcolombo"
  version="2026.09.03.8"
  launch="Settings/DockTail"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/main/plugin/docktail.plg"
  support="https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/issues"
  min="7.0.0"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[

### 2026.09.03.8

Fixes the exposed-port list on the Labels tab.

A container publishing a port range printed every number, running to several lines. Consecutive runs now collapse (e.g. `50000-50100`) and the list is capped with a '+N more' tail; the port dropdown still offers every individual port.

### 2026.09.03.7

Reworks the Labels tab.

- Picking a container now prefills a suggested service name, lists the ports it exposes, and loads any DockTail labels it already carries so you edit rather than start over.
- The output is the complete Extra Parameters value: your existing arguments with only the DockTail labels replaced. Paste over the whole field instead of merging by hand.
- Basic/Advanced split - four fields by default, the rest behind Unraid's Advanced View switch.
- Regenerates as you type, and validation errors appear in their own block instead of inside the output box.
- Copy now confirms itself and uses the modern clipboard API.

### 2026.09.03.6

Fixes settings not saving.

Apply appeared to do nothing and changes were lost on reload. Unraid validates the CSRF token centrally in its auto_prepend_file and then removes it from $_POST, so the plugin's own second check could only ever fail - answering 403 into the hidden frame the form targeted, invisibly. Generate on the Labels tab and Refresh on the DockTail tab failed the same way.

- Settings now save whatever you enter, including with Enable DockTail set to No.
- Apply reports its outcome next to the button instead of posting into a hidden frame.
- Generate and Refresh work again.


For older releases, see https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.8-noarch-1.txz">
<URL>https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases/download/2026.09.03.8/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.8-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>899951e0d25351e390b139e160beada9f65bd4df770996898f9c38bb7bebf208</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script. Unraid re-installs every /boot/config/plugins/*.plg on
boot, so this runs at boot too: it must be idempotent and must not fail when
Docker or Tailscale are still down.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
if [ -d "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail" ]; then
    rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
fi

upgradepkg --install-new /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.03.8-noarch-1.txz

mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/docktail

# Keep tailnet credentials out of Unraid Connect's flash backup, which is a git
# repo at /boot/.git.
echo "credentials.cfg" > /boot/config/plugins/docktail/.gitignore

if [ ! -f "/boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg" ]; then
    install -m 0600 /dev/null /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg
fi
chmod 0600 /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg

# Drop the other release channel so both are never installed at once.
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail-preview.plg
rm -f /var/log/plugins/docktail-preview.plg

# Start (or restart) the daemon. Deferred, so a blocking Unraid event returns
# immediately.
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail/restart.sh

# Clean up superseded packages.
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '2026.09.03.8')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " docktail has been installed."
echo " Plugin version:   2026.09.03.8"
echo " DockTail version: 1.7.9"
echo ""
echo " Configure it under Settings -> Network Services ->"
echo " DockTail. DockTail needs the Tailscale plugin and a"
echo " tagged Unraid node; the Status tab checks both."
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script. Settings under /boot/config/plugins/docktail are left in place:
Unraid convention is that plugin settings survive removal.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
/usr/local/etc/rc.d/rc.docktail stop 2>/dev/null

removepkg docktail-unraid

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail/*.txz
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
